 NEXORA chain id, if the id is already registered, or if the supplied type and key do not reproduce `assetId` on this chain.\",\"assetType\":\"the asset type, which is re-derived and checked\"}}},\"version\":1},\"userdoc\":{\"errors\":{\"AidChainMismatch(uint256,uint256)\":[{\"notice\":\"Workbench addition for SPEC \\u00a74.1 enforcement in on-chain consumers.         Canonical tracked aid/src/Aid.sol does not declare this error; the         corrected workbench AidRegistry uses it for chain-id mismatch reverts.\"}]},\"kind\":\"user\",\"methods\":{\"assetIdAt(uint256)\":{\"notice\":\"The nth identifier ever registered, including retracted ones.\"},\"configuredChainId()\":{\"notice\":\"Exposes the configured chain id for off-chain checks/tests.\"},\"paginate(uint256,uint256)\":{\"notice\":\"Every registered entry at `from`, up to `max` entries. Cursor pagination.\"},\"register(bytes32,uint8,bytes32)\":{\"notice\":\"Files a claim for `assetId` on the actual chain.\"},\"retract(bytes32)\":{\"notice\":\"Retracts a claim. Only the original registrant may do this, and a retraction         is final: the identifier cannot be claimed again.\"},\"verify(bytes32,bytes32)\":{\"notice\":\"Verifies a stored entry against the identifier scheme on the actual chain. Returns false for non-registered/retracted entries, wrong asset key, or wrong chain context. Reverts if block.chainid is not the configured NEXORA chain id.\"}},\"notice\":\"NEXORA Asset Identifier Registry \\u2014 minimal, TESTNET workbench correction. PROVENANCE / CORRECTION (2026-11-07, workbench only) ---------------------------------------------------- Derived from `source/aid/src/AidRegistry.sol` (canonical, tracked). The canonical implementation takes a caller-supplied `uint256 chainId` in `register`/`verify` and passes it to `Aid.assetId(...)`. `aid/SPEC.md` \\u00a74.1 states: \\\"A contract must not trust a caller-supplied chain id. It reads `block.chainid`, and must verify that value against its own configured constant, failing loudly on mismatch rather than minting identifiers into the wrong domain.\\\" This workbench copy corrects that semantic issue for an explicitly TESTNET-only deployment on NEXORA devnet (EVM chain id 902024):   - removes caller-supplied `chainId` from state-changing/verification entrypoints;   - reads `block.chainid`;   - requires `block.chainid == CONFIGURED_CHAIN_ID` (902024), reverting with     `Aid.AidChainMismatch` on mismatch/fork/foreign deployment;   - computes identifiers only for the actual chain. NOT a canonical source edit. NOT audited. `aid/SPEC.md` remains DRAFT (Solidity cross-check of all vectors and \\u00a710 decisions open). Deploy/test on isolated loopback local testnet only. WHAT THIS IS NOT ---------------- Registering here does NOT attest that an asset exists, that the registrar controls it, or that its code matches its declared type. `aid/SPEC.md` \\u00a73 is explicit that an `assetId` is an identifier and not a claim about the world; this contract stores a *claim* and says so. WHAT IT DOES GUARANTEE ---------------------- 1. **The metadata hashes to the identifier it is filed under, for the actual chain.**    Every registration recomputes `assetId(block.chainid, assetType, assetKey)` after    verifying `block.chainid` equals the configured NEXORA EVM chain id, and reverts if    it does not equal the id being registered. 2. **First claim wins, permanently.** A registered identifier cannot be overwritten. 3. **Only the original registrant can retract.** Deregistration is a statement by the    party that made the claim, not by a third party. 4. **Wrong-chain/fork deployment fails loudly.** Operations revert if `block.chainid`    is not the configured constant. There is no owner, no upgrade path, and no pause.\",\"version\":1}},\"settings\":{\"compilationTarget\":{\"src/AidRegistry.sol\":\"AidRegistry\"},\"evmVersion\":\"cancun\",\"libraries\":{},\"metadata\":{\"bytecodeHash\":\"ipfs\"},\"optimizer\":{\"enabled\":true,\"runs\":200},\"remappings\":[]},\"sources\":{\"src/Aid.sol\":{\"keccak256\":\"0xde7d16f2c064a40bb3977a1e12d154364218f4e2658f1fd8ea6201bac95c3117\",\"license\":\"MIT\",\"urls\":[\"bzz-raw://400a16c344e62d31035cc400ab8d7fa47e536f6fa0ded5c29364cc49ef9cc88f\",\"dweb:/ipfs/QmXDAxtUvneSigsr8yiaFZpZftwUXmUyFyEj1JVRhdZ9cb\"]},\"src/AidRegistry.sol\":{\"keccak256\":\"0x004542a57eba59ecc0a8f1f30d1fca0e221c6c191445590018c30c841e5b8822\",\"license\":\"MIT\",\"urls\":[\"bzz-raw://313de9bb9a1a15d82590e86acadb383da5d5e05ccd24c8e93c4744bc0f045a2d\",\"dweb:/ipfs/QmTmWCYDdx1qb2YxMVohknbbjPNobhAYYxhFc3HpG4cUvA\"]}},\"version\":1}","metadata":{"compiler":{"version":"0.8.24+commit.e11b9ed9"},"language":"Solidity","output":{"abi":[{"inputs":[{"internalType":"bytes32","name":"assetId","type":"bytes32"}],"type":"error","name":"AidAlreadyRegistered"},{"inputs":[{"internalType":"uint256","name":"expected","type":"uint256"},{"internalType":"uint256","name":"actual","type":"uint256"}],"type":"error","name":"AidChainMismatch"},{"inputs":[{"internalType":"bytes32","name":"claimed","type":"bytes32"},{"internalType":"bytes32","name":"computed","type":"bytes32"}],"type":"error","name":"AidMetadataDoesNotMatchIdentifier"},{"inputs":[{"internalType":"bytes32","name":"assetId","type":"bytes32"}],"type":"error","name":"AidNotRegistered"},{"inputs":[{"internalType":"bytes32","name":"assetId","type":"bytes32"},{"internalType":"address","name":"caller","type":"address"}],"type":"error","name":"AidNotTheRegistrant"},{"inputs":[],"type":"error","name":"AidUnknownSpecVersion"},{"inputs":[{"internalType":"uint8","name":"assetType","type":"uint8"}],"type":"error","name":"AidUnknownType"},{"inputs":[],"type":"error","name":"AidZeroRegistrant"},{"inputs":[{"internalType":"bytes32","name":"assetId","type":"bytes32","indexed":true},{"internalType":"uint8","name":"assetType","type":"uint8","indexed":true},{"internalType":"address","name":"registrant","type":"address","indexed":true}],"type":"event","name":"Registered","anony